ng &lt;dongseong.hwang@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dongseong Hwang &lt;dongseong.hwang@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Gurchetan Singh &lt;gurchetansingh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="339190" owner_email="dongseong.hwang@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="18" project="chromiumos/platform/drm-tests" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/drm-tests" ref="refs/changes/90/339190/18" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I98777c5ab738f3e9fc27880546e6afcf808fe11a" commit="a38a9dd061a5ebcbc8a3bbade6ea0a1c1eb50a50" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Enable CONFIG_IP6_NF_MATCH_RPFILTER  netd creates an ip6tables rule that requires the rpfilter match module for IPv6.  Without this module, the operation fails.  BUG=chromium:696865 TEST=start an Android VPN, and then run in android-sh:      ndc ipfwd enable tethering      ndc ipfwd add arc0 tun0      ndc nat enable arc0 tun0 0 TEST=`ip6tables -w -t raw -A PREROUTING -i br0 -m rpfilter \       --invert '!' -s fe80::/64 -j DROP`  Change-Id: I98777c5ab738f3e9fc27880546e6afcf808fe11a Signed-off-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/447303 Reviewed-by: Kirtika Ruchandani &lt;kirtika@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="5" gerrit_number="447303" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/03/447303/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5b71464cef9541edffecb5195df9fb16d00c37ce" commit="8889d06b30fb868eeea154103dcc4003aa8472cc" commit_message="power_state: add ccd_reset command  Servo currently cannot recover any of the stm32 usb endpoints if there is a usb reset.  For Cr50 testing we may need to reset Cr50 or disconnect CCD momentarily. This will lead to a USB reset.  This change ccd_reset to power state which will reinitialize all servo interfaces when called. For ccd this means that each usb endpoint will be reset.  With this change all interfaces with &quot;reinitialize&quot; methods will reinitialize when &quot;power_state:ccd_reset&quot; is called. Any reinitialize methods should be implemented so that they don't break anything if the interface is already running.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57468 BRANCH=none TEST=connect suzyq or servo v4 to dut. start servod using ccd. disconnect suzyq and reconnect it. run dut-control ccd_reset_usb:on and then run dut-control and verify all of the fields are populated. verify all of the consoles work.  Change-Id: I5b71464cef9541edffecb5195df9fb16d00c37ce Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/445926 Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="445926" owner_email="mruthven@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/26/445926/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id725e97b6d726fdf68c063582d45c640d4541bbe" commit="8019ffa6b3a520f0c18fe21fdc1fa9e6dbd602c2" commit_message="[autotest] Use AfeHostInfoStore to obtain host information in test_push  This is not really needed to remove autoserv dependencies on the AFE, but this allows us to remove the duplicated functions in site_utils.  BUG=chromium:678430 TEST=test_push  Change-Id: Id725e97b6d726fdf68c063582d45c640d4541bbe Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/442656 Commit-Ready: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="442656" owner_email="pprabhu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" 